luci-app-fleth — https://github.com/makeding/luci-app-fleth

The MAP-E rule tables in mape_rules.go are generated from
root/usr/sbin/fleth-map-e.lua, and the calculation in mape.go is a port of the same
file. That file is authored by huggy <fleth@huggy.moe> and rewritten there from
https://ipv4.web.fc2.com/map-e.html; the tables themselves are measurements
contributed by the Japanese IPoE community and collated by that project.

The GPL-2.0 exception luci-app-fleth states for root/lib/netifd/proto/ipip6h.sh and
htdocs/luci-static/resources/protocol/ipip6h.js does not apply here: sixup uses neither
file. What it uses is covered by the MIT licence below.

